{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-104458" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The cubic polynomial $P(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=-3,$ ${x}_{2}=-2,$ and ${x}_{3}=3,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $4.$ Find $P(x).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981281/state.json" "file_sha256" "3d429f4182075afe8ff59b1af29627084f4c760cb3c330faa79637b60c63bdd0"} {"question" "q-104458" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since our cubic polynomial has roots ${x}_{1}=-3,$ ${x}_{1}=-2,$ and ${x}_{3}=3,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=4,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) & =4(x-(-3))(x-(-2))(x-3) \\\\  & =4(x+3)(x+2)(x-3)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(x+3)(x+2)(x-3) & =4({x}^{2}+5x+6)(x-3) \\\\  & =4({x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}+5{x}^{2}-15x+6x-18) \\\\  & =4({x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}-9x-18) \\\\  & =4{x}^{3}+8{x}^{2}-36x-72.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)=4{x}^{3}+8{x}^{2}-36x-72.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981281/state.json" "file_sha256" "3d429f4182075afe8ff59b1af29627084f4c760cb3c330faa79637b60c63bdd0"} {"question" "q-104458" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981281/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "84105d3e3c2789c6fb700d3bfd509a862a2e8fa15a9f73cee39754341118d6c3"} {"question" "q-104458" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981281/state.json" "file_sha256" "3d429f4182075afe8ff59b1af29627084f4c760cb3c330faa79637b60c63bdd0"} {"question" "q-104458" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "4{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}-18x-36"] ["math" "4{x}^{3}+8{x}^{2}-36x-18"] ["math" "4{x}^{3}+8{x}^{2}-36x-72"] ["math" "4{x}^{3}+8{x}^{2}-9x-18"] ["math" "4{x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}+18x-72"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981281/state.json" "file_sha256" "3d429f4182075afe8ff59b1af29627084f4c760cb3c330faa79637b60c63bdd0"} {"question" "q-104458" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4{x}^{3}+8{x}^{2}-36x-72"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981281/state.json" "file_sha256" "3d429f4182075afe8ff59b1af29627084f4c760cb3c330faa79637b60c63bdd0"} {"question" "q-316619" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The cubic polynomial $P(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=1,$ ${x}_{2}=-3,$ and ${x}_{3}=4,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $5.$ Find $P(x).$\n\n$P(x)=$\n{{field-1}}${x}^{3}\\,-$\n{{field-2}}${x}^{2}\\,-$\n{{field-3}}$x\\,+$\n{{field-4}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981281/state.json" "file_sha256" "3d429f4182075afe8ff59b1af29627084f4c760cb3c330faa79637b60c63bdd0"} {"question" "q-316619" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since our cubic polynomial has roots ${x}_{1}=1,$ ${x}_{2}=-3,$ and ${x}_{3}=4,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=5,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) & =5(x-1)(x-(-3))(x-4) \\\\  & =5(x-1)(x+3)(x-4)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5(x-1)(x+3)(x-4) & =5({x}^{2}+2x-3)(x-4) \\\\  & =5({x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}+2{x}^{2}-8x-3x+12) \\\\  & =5({x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}-11x+12) \\\\  & =5{x}^{3}-10{x}^{2}-55x+60.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)=5{x}^{3}-10{x}^{2}-55x+60.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981281/state.json" "file_sha256" "3d429f4182075afe8ff59b1af29627084f4c760cb3c330faa79637b60c63bdd0"} {"question" "q-316619" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981281/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "84105d3e3c2789c6fb700d3bfd509a862a2e8fa15a9f73cee39754341118d6c3"} {"question" "q-316619" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981281/state.json" "file_sha256" "3d429f4182075afe8ff59b1af29627084f4c760cb3c330faa79637b60c63bdd0"} {"question" "q-316619" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981281/state.json" "file_sha256" "3d429f4182075afe8ff59b1af29627084f4c760cb3c330faa79637b60c63bdd0"} {"question" "q-316619" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981281/state.json" "file_sha256" "3d429f4182075afe8ff59b1af29627084f4c760cb3c330faa79637b60c63bdd0"} {"question" "q-316619" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "10"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981281/state.json" "file_sha256" "3d429f4182075afe8ff59b1af29627084f4c760cb3c330faa79637b60c63bdd0"} {"question" "q-316619" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981281/state.json" "file_sha256" "3d429f4182075afe8ff59b1af29627084f4c760cb3c330faa79637b60c63bdd0"} {"question" "q-316619" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "55"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981281/state.json" "file_sha256" "3d429f4182075afe8ff59b1af29627084f4c760cb3c330faa79637b60c63bdd0"} {"question" "q-316619" "field" "field-4" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981281/state.json" "file_sha256" "3d429f4182075afe8ff59b1af29627084f4c760cb3c330faa79637b60c63bdd0"} {"question" "q-316619" "field" "field-4" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "60"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981281/state.json" "file_sha256" "3d429f4182075afe8ff59b1af29627084f4c760cb3c330faa79637b60c63bdd0"} {"question" "q-316621" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The cubic polynomial $P(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=-4,{x}_{3}=1,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $2.$ Find $P(x).$\n\n$P(x)=$\n{{field-1}}${x}^{3}\\,+$\n{{field-2}}${x}^{2}\\,+$\n{{field-3}}$x\\,-$\n{{field-4}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981281/state.json" "file_sha256" "3d429f4182075afe8ff59b1af29627084f4c760cb3c330faa79637b60c63bdd0"} {"question" "q-316621" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since our cubic polynomial has roots ${x}_{1}=-4,$ ${x}_{2}=-4,$ and ${x}_{3}=1,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=2,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) & =2(x-(-4))(x-(-4))(x-1) \\\\  & =2(x+4)(x+4)(x-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(x+4)(x+4)(x-1) & =2({x}^{2}+8x+16)(x-1) \\\\  & =2({x}^{3}-{x}^{2}+8{x}^{2}-8x+16x-16) \\\\  & =2({x}^{3}+7{x}^{2}+8x-16) \\\\  & =2{x}^{3}+14{x}^{2}+16x-32.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)=2{x}^{3}+14{x}^{2}+16x-32.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981281/state.json" "file_sha256" "3d429f4182075afe8ff59b1af29627084f4c760cb3c330faa79637b60c63bdd0"} {"question" "q-316621" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981281/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "84105d3e3c2789c6fb700d3bfd509a862a2e8fa15a9f73cee39754341118d6c3"} {"question" "q-316621" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981281/state.json" "file_sha256" "3d429f4182075afe8ff59b1af29627084f4c760cb3c330faa79637b60c63bdd0"} {"question" "q-316621" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981281/state.json" "file_sha256" "3d429f4182075afe8ff59b1af29627084f4c760cb3c330faa79637b60c63bdd0"} {"question" "q-316621" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981281/state.json" "file_sha256" "3d429f4182075afe8ff59b1af29627084f4c760cb3c330faa79637b60c63bdd0"} {"question" "q-316621" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "14"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981281/state.json" "file_sha256" "3d429f4182075afe8ff59b1af29627084f4c760cb3c330faa79637b60c63bdd0"} {"question" "q-316621" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981281/state.json" "file_sha256" "3d429f4182075afe8ff59b1af29627084f4c760cb3c330faa79637b60c63bdd0"} {"question" "q-316621" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "16"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981281/state.json" "file_sha256" "3d429f4182075afe8ff59b1af29627084f4c760cb3c330faa79637b60c63bdd0"} {"question" "q-316621" "field" "field-4" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981281/state.json" "file_sha256" "3d429f4182075afe8ff59b1af29627084f4c760cb3c330faa79637b60c63bdd0"} {"question" "q-316621" "field" "field-4" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "32"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981281/state.json" "file_sha256" "3d429f4182075afe8ff59b1af29627084f4c760cb3c330faa79637b60c63bdd0"} {"question" "q-316649" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The cubic polynomial $f(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=-5,{x}_{2,3}=\\pm 2\\text{i},$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $5.$ Find $f(x).$\n\n$f(x)=$\n{{field-1}}${x}^{3}\\,+$\n{{field-2}}${x}^{2}\\,+$\n{{field-3}}$x\\,+$\n{{field-4}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981281/state.json" "file_sha256" "3d429f4182075afe8ff59b1af29627084f4c760cb3c330faa79637b60c63bdd0"} {"question" "q-316649" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since $f(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=-5$ and ${x}_{2,3}=\\pm 2\\text{i},$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=5,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) \\\\  & =5(x-(-5))(x-2\\text{i})(x-(-2\\text{i})) \\\\  & =5(x+5)(x-2\\text{i})(x+2\\text{i})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5(x+5)(x-2\\text{i})(x+2\\text{i}) & = \\\\ 5(x+5)({x}^{2}-(2\\text{i})^{2}) & = \\\\ 5(x+5)({x}^{2}+4) & = \\\\ 5({x}^{3}+5{x}^{2}+4x+20) & = \\\\ 5{x}^{3}+25{x}^{2}+20x+100 & .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)=5{x}^{3}+25{x}^{2}+20x+100.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981281/state.json" "file_sha256" "3d429f4182075afe8ff59b1af29627084f4c760cb3c330faa79637b60c63bdd0"} {"question" "q-316649" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981281/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "84105d3e3c2789c6fb700d3bfd509a862a2e8fa15a9f73cee39754341118d6c3"} {"question" "q-316649" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981281/state.json" "file_sha256" "3d429f4182075afe8ff59b1af29627084f4c760cb3c330faa79637b60c63bdd0"} {"question" "q-316649" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981281/state.json" "file_sha256" "3d429f4182075afe8ff59b1af29627084f4c760cb3c330faa79637b60c63bdd0"} {"question" "q-316649" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Acade